MID_EV20_022_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_022_m01_001: We have lost Grand Aragon? You can't be serious.
MID_EV20_022_m01_002: The Alliance was meant to be pinned down at\nAgris Stronghold.
MID_EV20_022_m01_003: We gather that they used a small, elite force to act\nbefore we were ready.
MID_EV20_022_m01_004: If Arago has fallen into enemy hands, their\nremaining forces may join the Alliance.
MID_EV20_022_m01_005: Mobilizing to seize Arago under our noses is bolder\nthan I credited them for.
MID_EV20_022_m01_006: The human vermin win this round.
MID_EV20_022_m01_007: We anticipate a push from the Alliance now that\ntheir flank is clear of threats.
MID_EV20_022_m01_008: Hm. I concur.
MID_EV20_022_m01_009: Magistra Raksha? The residents of hightown have\nbeen executed as you asked.
MID_EV20_022_m01_010: Counting them, we have sacrificed approximately\nhalf the humans in Dagsion.
MID_EV20_022_m01_011: Well done. Continue processing those who are left,\ndistrict by district.
MID_EV20_022_m01_012: Ah... Mm...
MID_EV20_022_m01_013: Yes, Hong Hua? Is there something you'd like to say?
MID_EV20_022_m01_014: Magistra Raksha, I have always been faithful to you.\nI owe you a great debt for saving me long ago.
MID_EV20_022_m01_015: But I also hoped it would lead to my revenge against\nDagda the Great.
MID_EV20_022_m01_016: Ah, yes...you owe him for the Battle of Fezzan.\nWhere your husband died and your child was stolen.
MID_EV20_022_m01_017: Fear not. I keep my promises, and Dagda the Great\nis far along the road to ruin.
MID_EV20_022_m01_018: Yes, but... Is this really the way to achieve it?
MID_EV20_022_m01_019: Poor Hong Hua. You are our last remaining Guardian\nof the Compass.
MID_EV20_022_m01_020: The toll on you must be heavy indeed. Allow me to\nease that burden.
MID_EV20_022_m01_021: You may delegate the executions to someone else\nand rest for now.
MID_EV20_022_m01_022: A-ah. Thank you.
MID_EV20_022_m01_023: I...I can't seem to stop shaking. Is it from fear?
MID_EV20_022_m01_024: What have I been a part of all this time?
MID_EV20_022_m01_025: The things I've done...were they justified?
MID_EV20_022_m01_026: Hmph.
MID_EV20_022_m01_027: I fear she may be lost to us for good.
MID_EV20_022_m01_028: Can we allow that, Magistra?
MID_EV20_022_m01_029: Hong Hua's contributions have bought her that much\ngrace, at least. As a parting gift, I grant her her life.
MID_EV20_022_m01_030: Lind is still at Alcineus Span. All we need from him\nis a small amount of time.
MID_EV20_022_m01_031: If he can hold the Alliance at bay, the plan will\nproceed. And he is in a good position to do so.
MID_EV20_022_m01_032: Let us forget Hong Hua. There is nothing she can\ndo to hinder us.
MID_EV20_022_m01_033: Not when our preparations are nearly complete.\nWe need only to await the finishing touches.
MID_NR20_09_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_09_m01_001: Word spread across the land that something was\nterribly wrong in Dagsion—but what exactly, nobody\nknew. People shared the rumors with horror.
MID_NR20_09_m01_002: One rumor said that not a single letter sent there had\ngotten a reply. Another, that not one merchant had\ngone in or out. A third, that all entries were blocked.
MID_NR20_09_m01_003: Some people even began to say that Dagsion—the\ncity itself—had gone silent. And that was perhaps\nthe most troubling rumor of all.
MID_NR20_09_m01_004: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 4, Chapter 1
MID_EV20_023_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_023_m01_001: So the situation within Dagsion remains unknown.
MID_EV20_023_m01_084: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_085: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_086: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_087: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_088: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_089: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_090: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_091: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_092: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_093: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_094: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_095: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_096: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_097: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_098: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_002: I asked staff from the temples of Jurah and Kalla\nto bring us any word they could.
MID_EV20_023_m01_003: But the Gates of the Gods seem to have been closed\nfrom the Dagsion side.
MID_EV20_023_m01_004: And unfortunately, that means we have no way to\nfind out what's going on.
MID_EV20_023_m01_005: It's a stone's throw away, yet we have no idea what\nthings are like in there. Very frustrating.
MID_EV20_023_m01_006: What could be happening in that city?
MID_EV20_023_m01_007: I dunno, boss. Maybe it's some strategy where\neveryone inside is laying low?
MID_EV20_023_m01_008: It is possible...but this does not feel like an enemy\nbaiting a trap. All is eerily quiet.
MID_EV20_023_m01_009: There is a well-worn tactic known as the\nempty-fort strategy.
MID_EV20_023_m01_010: By making a fort appear empty, the stratagem causes\nwarriors to lower their guards or jump at shadows.
MID_EV20_023_m01_011: I doubt that is what we are seeing. What would it\nbenefit them to do this?
MID_EV20_023_m01_012: I cannot fathom the Divine Emperor's intentions.\nIt is unsettling.
MID_EV20_023_m01_013: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_014: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_015: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_016: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_017: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_018: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_019: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_020: Reconnaissance is called for here. We must know\nwhat is happening in Dagsion.
MID_EV20_023_m01_021: But our immediate problem is Alcineus Span.
MID_EV20_023_m01_022: I tried a few approaches on the board, but Dagsion\nis fortified enough to repel all of them.
MID_EV20_023_m01_023: Yes, I designed it that way. Erm...sorry about that.
MID_EV20_023_m01_024: Never did I dream that one day I would have to\noutsmart myself in assaulting it.
MID_EV20_023_m01_025: Understandable. No one here blames you, I am sure.
MID_EV20_023_m01_026: I feel a little better, hearing you say that.
MID_EV20_023_m01_027: Queen Theodora, we may be at war, but our enemy's\nsoldiers are only human.
MID_EV20_023_m01_028: They must be longing for some entertainment,\ncooped up in that city.
MID_EV20_023_m01_029: Is the idea that we act as traveling entertainers to\ninfiltrate them? Because I'm on board.
MID_EV20_023_m01_030: I have my doubts. General Lind is a stranger man\nthan you might imagine.
MID_EV20_023_m01_031: According to our captives, his tastes in recreation\nare monstrous.
MID_EV20_023_m01_032: We cannot allow you to be taken hostage and\ninterrogated. You know far too much.
MID_EV20_023_m01_033: I would prefer that you perform here instead to raise\nour warriors' morale.
MID_EV20_023_m01_034: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_035: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_036: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_037: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_038: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_039: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_040: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_041: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_042: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_043: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_044: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_045: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_046: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_047: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_048: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_049: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_050: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_051: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_052: 
MID_EV20_023_m01_053: It denies us no matter what we attempt. What an\nobstinate city.
MID_EV20_023_m01_054: Indeed. The only place this difficult to siege would\nbe Garreg Mach of Fódlan.
MID_EV20_023_m01_055: Don't we have more than a hundred thousand\nsoldiers?
MID_EV20_023_m01_056: Can't we just push through? We're right at the gates!
MID_EV20_023_m01_057: Indeed not. There are many reasons, but I will name\nonly one.
MID_EV20_023_m01_058: Supply lines. Have you heard of them?
MID_EV20_023_m01_059: Sure, I know that much. That's how provisions are\nmoved to the camps.
MID_EV20_023_m01_060: Securing them is critical in battles with large armies.
MID_EV20_023_m01_061: It would take a week for a wagon to arrive here from \nour base at Agris Stronghold.
MID_EV20_023_m01_062: If the enemy could disrupt our resupply... Our forces\nwould collapse.
MID_EV20_023_m01_063: Yet our enemy has no such weakness. Holed up in\nDagsion, their stockpiles are enormous.
MID_EV20_023_m01_064: Now I see. I've got to hand it to you, Fabio. You\nare smart.
MID_EV20_023_m01_065: My thirst for battle is fierce. This war will quench it\nsoon, I hope.
MID_EV20_023_m01_066: Yes, I suspect you will get your drink soon enough.
MID_EV20_023_m01_067: I think the queen herself has no more patience than\nyou do.
MID_EV20_023_m01_068: Now, in war, nothing affects the outcome like the\nsoldiers' morale.
MID_EV20_023_m01_069: Our Saramis-Brezarant Alliance has a leg up on the\nenemy as far as that goes.
MID_EV20_023_m01_070: In contrast, I'm not sure the empire's forces arrayed\nagainst us quite know what they're fighting for.
MID_EV20_023_m01_071: Right. I can't bring myself to agree with the\nDivine Emperor's way of doing things.
MID_EV20_023_m01_072: And anyway, now that we've come this far, we don't\nhave any other options.
MID_EV20_023_m01_073: Right you are, Cai. I pledge to support your alliance\nin any way that I can.
MID_EV20_023_m01_074: All my life, I've been too timid to stand up to\nmy father.
MID_EV20_023_m01_075: It's made me complicit in many things I would rather\nnot have happened. But no more.
MID_EV20_023_m01_076: Mom said that you know how to get things done,\nUncle Credna.
MID_EV20_023_m01_077: Aurora said that? I'm delighted to hear it.
MID_EV20_023_m01_078: The tide of battle does seem to flow in our favor.
MID_EV20_023_m01_079: Yes. There's nothing more to fear behind us, so we\ncan confront the enemy head on.
MID_EV20_023_m01_080: They have a saying in Sai that "a miracle fallen from\nthe heavens cannot match a mastery of the earth."
MID_EV20_023_m01_081: But there's more to it. "A mastery of the earth cannot\ntriumph over a union of souls."
MID_EV20_023_m01_082: It means that no matter how sound your strategy is,\nit's doomed to fail against a united front.
MID_EV20_023_m01_083: It is good to be reminded of this. As our hearts are\none, we are bound for victory.
MID_EV20_103_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_103_m01_001: Mind if I sit?
MID_EV20_103_m01_002: Pretty horrid display. Even the sound... You're the\none they're calling the Lord of Impalement, then?
MID_EV20_103_m01_003: Hmph.
MID_EV20_103_m01_004: By the looks of it, these aren't just captured enemies.\nYou've got your deserters out there, and civilians too.
MID_EV20_103_m01_005: So what is it? Everyone gets the stake, young or old?\nYou unscrupulous devil.
MID_EV20_103_m01_006: Death is impartial. It's the one rule of the world, and\nnot even Dagda the Great can defy it.
MID_EV20_103_m01_007: These impaled wretches are on display to show what\ncomes of disobeying me.
MID_EV20_103_m01_008: As much as I want to hate you, I can't help but feel\na certain kinship between us. How strange.
MID_EV20_103_m01_009: You look younger than I'd expect over five hundred\nyears after Vandahl's death.
MID_EV20_103_m01_010: So even the Lord of Impalement's heard of me.\nI'm honored.
MID_EV20_103_m01_011: I myself was the bastard son of the hero Arago\nand Jurah.
MID_EV20_103_m01_012: Oh?
MID_EV20_103_m01_013: I hid my parentage to serve Dagda the Great. I came\nto be known as the Baneful Knight.
MID_EV20_103_m01_014: My new liege wasn't pleased when he noticed how\nstrong my feelings for my mother were.
MID_EV20_103_m01_015: He sentenced me to a thousand years of isolation for\nit. Only now do I have a moment of freedom.
MID_EV20_103_m01_016: That'd make you and me cousins, no?
MID_EV20_103_m01_017: And that would make you...three-quarters god?
MID_EV20_103_m01_018: What does that matter? Is the same true of you?
MID_EV20_103_m01_019: I'd rather discuss what you hope to gain here. I love\nlearning what drives people, you see—as a merchant.
MID_EV20_103_m01_020: Love, that's all. When I win this war, I'll have\nMother's love again.
MID_EV20_103_m01_021: Huh. We may have more in common than blood.
MID_EV20_103_m01_022: Hm? Most people find it strange when I speak of\nthese things.
MID_EV20_103_m01_023: I know how it feels to miss your mom. I searched for\nmine my entire life. And when I finally found her...
MID_EV20_103_m01_024: Well... Long story short, she's dead now—and I'm the\none who killed her. Fun stuff, I know.
MID_EV20_103_m01_025: I see. You've faced your own struggles, then.
MID_EV20_103_m01_026: She never wanted me in her life. She'd have\npreferred I was never born.
MID_EV20_103_m01_027: She didn't even love my old man. Her heart belonged\nto someone else all along.
MID_EV20_103_m01_028: Now here I am, like you, another poor child starved\nof his mother's love.
MID_EV20_103_m01_029: With her dead, I don't know how I'll ever fill\nthis emptiness.
MID_EV20_103_m01_030: You still haven't told me why you're here.
MID_EV20_103_m01_031: I'm here for the sake of my own considerable\ninterests, I assure you.
MID_EV20_103_m01_032: I wouldn't be dancing to Old Man Dagda's tune\nif I had another choice.
MID_EV20_103_m01_033: Throwing in with him seemed like the best bet.\nAnd now that I'm in, I've staked it all—even my life.
MID_EV20_103_m01_034: That's the only way to play it. No turning back.
MID_EV20_103_m01_035: If you're always changing direction with the wind,\nyou'll end up lost at sea.
MID_EV20_103_m01_036: That's another thing the two of us have in common.
MID_EV20_103_m01_037: Exactly. Even if we don't see eye to eye, if we can\nagree on that, no reason we can't work together.
MID_EV20_103_m01_038: What about your friends in the enemy ranks?
MID_EV20_103_m01_039: Well, it's like I said, cousin. I'm already a seasoned\nhand at killing people close to me.
MID_NR20_05_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_05_m01_001: The elite force rejoined the main army after seizing\nGrand Aragon, bringing with it Arago's remaining\ntroops. Together, they marched on Alcineus Span.
MID_NR20_05_m01_002: What first greeted the Alliance as they drew near\nwas the sight of innumerable birds blotting out\nthe sky, followed by an unbearable stench.
MID_NR20_05_m01_003: Soon enough, they saw the bridge itself. Along its\nlength, corpses stood impaled upon stakes. The birds\ncircling above had been feasting upon them. What\nthe army had marched into was a hellish scene.
MID_NR20_05_m01_004: The Baneful Knight Lind stood forth as Theodora's\narmy approached. The general—most feared of the\nDagdan Empire—smiled ominously.
MID_NR20_05_m01_005: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 4, Chapter 5
MID_EV20_024_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_024_m01_001: What is this foul odor? The battle has not yet\neven begun.
MID_EV20_024_m01_013: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_061: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_062: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_063: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_064: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_065: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_066: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_067: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_068: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_069: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_070: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_071: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_072: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_073: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_002: That's the scent of death. Notice how it gets stronger\nas we approach the bridge.
MID_EV20_024_m01_003: To smell it at this distance says nothing good for\nour enemy's commander.
MID_EV20_024_m01_004: Something's not right. Dagsion seems...off...somehow.
MID_EV20_024_m01_005: Peter, can you really see what's going on in the city\nfrom this far away?
MID_EV20_024_m01_006: Yeah, but it's more about what I don't see. There's\nmovement, but it's only windmills and waterwheels.
MID_EV20_024_m01_007: Oh! There's a bunch of stakes on the bridge.
MID_EV20_024_m01_008: The sky is filled with birds. Are they...waterfowl?
MID_EV20_024_m01_009: They are not. They visit Fódlan as well, and feed\non carrion.
MID_EV20_024_m01_010: You will see them flock after the fighting is done to\nseek corpse meat. To see them before is...peculiar.
MID_EV20_024_m01_011: Do you mean to say that the city already has a large\nstock of corpses?
MID_EV20_024_m01_012: There it is again—the detestable barbarism of beasts.
MID_EV20_024_m01_060: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_014: I had some notion of what to expect, and yet...
MID_EV20_024_m01_015: This forest of stakes and the victims impaled upon\nthem is a wrenching sight.
MID_EV20_024_m01_016: I cannot imagine such a thing... Can humans really\nbe so cruel?
MID_EV20_024_m01_017: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_018: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_019: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_020: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_021: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_022: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_023: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_024: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_025: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_026: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_027: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_028: Call it a warning. Or call it pageantry, if you like.
MID_EV20_024_m01_029: I find fear useful to bind a vast army together.
MID_EV20_024_m01_030: When I rout you here, your impaled corpses will\nadd to the effect.
MID_EV20_024_m01_031: They'll be out on display for all to see. For the birds\nto peck apart. For the winds to erode.
MID_EV20_024_m01_032: One look, and no one still living in the Dagdan\nEmpire will ever think to defy it again.
MID_EV20_024_m01_033: It's been a while since I had to face someone so\nnauseatingly evil.
MID_EV20_024_m01_034: I agree. It would be bad enough if he had just done\nthis to prisoners of war.
MID_EV20_024_m01_035: But some of them—they're in civilian garb. He was\nmaking an example out of them.
MID_EV20_024_m01_036: There is no excuse for this, no matter the authority\nsomeone has.
MID_EV20_024_m01_037: Plucking out lives in full bloom...then crushing\nthe petals. Horrible!
MID_EV20_024_m01_038: Lind of Dagda. You are as brutish as the tales say,\nif not more so.
MID_EV20_024_m01_039: You are a vision, queen of Saramis. Though your\nbeauty cannot compare to my mother's.
MID_EV20_024_m01_040: To honor you, I think I'll display your corpse so it's\nthe first thing any visitor to Alcineus Gate sees.
MID_EV20_024_m01_041: You depraved snake.
MID_EV20_024_m01_042: Life is emptiness. We eat, make waste, sleep,\nand leave nothing behind but corpses.
MID_EV20_024_m01_043: It's an unavoidable truth. We can pretend otherwise,\nbut there's no escaping death and the stink of decay.
MID_EV20_024_m01_044: We all rot in the end. Each and every one.
MID_EV20_024_m01_045: Your outlook is completely warped. All people\ndeserve to live happily and die with dignity.
MID_EV20_024_m01_046: Using their bodies as playthings... It's monstrous!\nYou will suffer for this.
MID_EV20_024_m01_047: Suffer? Suffering is a life that never ends.
MID_EV20_024_m01_048: Dagda the Great stuffed me away in a dark place for\nover five hundred years.
MID_EV20_024_m01_049: You can't imagine the agony of every second\nthat passes.
MID_EV20_024_m01_050: Next to that, I don't see what difference it makes\nhow a life of less than one hundred years ends.
MID_EV20_024_m01_051: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_052: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_053: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_054: 
MID_EV20_024_m01_055: I myself am a mere mortal in all respects. I can try\nto imagine what you speak of, but it is beyond me.
MID_EV20_024_m01_056: Tell me, did you grow twisted over these five\nhundred years, or was this always in your nature?
MID_EV20_024_m01_057: Surely you cannot be seeking sympathy from us.
MID_EV20_024_m01_058: It would matter not if you were. I have no desire to\ngrasp your craven outlook.
MID_EV20_024_m01_059: Well then, rebels against the empire. If the time for\nparley is past, let us turn to action.
MID_EV20_025_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_025_m01_001: I bring news. General Lind has been slain at\nAlcineus Span.
MID_EV20_025_m01_002: It seems the rebels have already opened\nAlcineus Gate.
MID_EV20_025_m01_003: They will surely flood into Dagsion soon.
MID_EV20_025_m01_004: So that noxious child Lind is finally dead, is he?
MID_EV20_025_m01_005: No matter. Even if he survived, I would have killed\nhim at some point.
MID_EV20_025_m01_006: But this Queen Theodora of Saramis...
MID_EV20_025_m01_007: She saved me the effort of killing Lind, which a\nhuman shouldn't have been able to do. Impressive.
MID_EV20_025_m01_008: Every last human in Dagsion has been converted\ninto flamma by now.
MID_EV20_025_m01_009: The batch we just brought in is the last of it.
MID_EV20_025_m01_010: Hm. Well done, Raksha.
MID_EV20_025_m01_011: Ahhh. Its overflowing strength seethes in me.\nMy dire wounds are fully healed.
MID_EV20_025_m01_012: I feel mightier than I ever have before!
MID_EV20_025_m01_013: Hmhmhm-hahaha!
MID_EV20_025_m01_014: With this flowing through me, I could crack the\nworld in two with a mere swipe of my arm!
MID_EV20_025_m01_015: This is...considerable power, even for me.
MID_EV20_025_m01_016: Very true. None in this world can hope to stand\nagainst Dagda the Great now.
MID_EV20_025_m01_017: Hah hah! Approach me if you dare, rebels.
MID_EV20_025_m01_018: I'll make you know such fear that your souls\nwill shrivel.